@* A reusable banner reminding readers that Blazor Server metrics describe the web host process, not the browser. *@

<div class="host-notice" role="note" aria-label="Important scope note">
    <span class="host-notice__icon" aria-hidden="true">i</span>
    <div class="host-notice__body">
        <strong>These metrics describe the server, not your browser.</strong>
        RuntimeMetricsLab.Web runs Blazor in <em>Interactive Server</em> mode, so all UI logic executes on
        the ASP.NET Core host. Every metric shown here — CPU time, GC/heap, thread pool, HTTP, sockets/TLS,
        gRPC, and custom OpenTelemetry counters — reflects the <strong>webfrontend</strong> or
        <strong>apiservice</strong> process on the server, never the browser tab's own CPU or memory usage.
    </div>
</div>
